        <cite>Arnab Kundu</cite>
        on <time datetime="2022-04-08 09:39:08.252236">April 08, 2022 at 09:39 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Related question: Is it true that a dimension <script type="math/tex">1</script> normal local domain is a valuation ring?</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-7311" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/00PD#comment-7311">Comment #7311</a>
        by
        <cite><a href="https://math.columbia.edu/~dejong" rel="author">Johan</a></cite>
        
        on <time datetime="2022-05-04 15:14:32.726025">May 04, 2022 at 15:14 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Don't know.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-11342" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/00PD#comment-11342">Comment #11342</a>
        by
        <cite><a href="https://stacks.math.columbia.edu" rel="author">stacks project</a></cite>
        
        on <time datetime="2026-04-14 13:09:13.679510">April 14, 2026 at 13:09 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Piotr Achinger send an example: If <script type="math/tex">K/k</script> is a nontrivial extension of fields with <script type="math/tex">k</script> algebraically closed in <script type="math/tex">K</script>, then the ring <script type="math/tex">R =\{f \in K[[x]] : f(0) \in k\}</script> is a local normal domain of dimension <script type="math/tex">1</script> but not a valuation ring.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-11609" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/00PD#comment-11609">Comment #11609</a>
        by
        <cite>Jakob Scholbach</cite>
        on <time datetime="2026-07-09 14:51:10.786930">July 09, 2026 at 14:51 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>I think in the very last sentence it should say every <em>nonzero</em> element of <script type="math/tex">A</script> can be written as <script type="math/tex">u \pi^n</script>...</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-11646" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/00PD#comment-11646">Comment #11646</a>
